Overview

Built a network-wide ad blocking and DNS filtering solution to improve browsing experience, reduce unwanted traffic, and gain hands-on experience with lightweight self-hosted services.

Components

Host Device | Raspberry Pi
Software | AdGuard Home
Storage | MicroSD Card
Networking | Static IP Configuration
Access Method | Web Management Interface
Role | Network DNS Filter

Process

Prepared the Raspberry Pi by flashing the operating system to a microSD card using an SD card reader. Installed and configured AdGuard Home as the primary DNS filtering service. Assigned a static IP address to ensure consistent network access. Updated router DNS settings so all devices on the network would use the new filtering server. Tested connectivity, DNS resolution, and ad blocking functionality across multiple devices.

